Minutes excerpt from the 2026-10-15 deviation investigation kickoff meeting (S-432 laboratory, 6 attendees):
1. The QC for batch B-42968 showed a systematic trend; 5 QC samples from the same batch decreased monotonically over time from 104.2% to 79.1%, a drift of 25.1 percentage points, and the last one was already below the 85% lower limit, with a coefficient of variation of 11.4% (acceptance limit 3.0%);
2. Of the 96 samples to be tested in the same batch, 12 were below the lower limit of quantification, a clear difference compared with 1 in the previous batch;
3. After reconstitution, the QC material was actually left for 5 hours 30 minutes, while the work procedure limit is 2 hours;
4. The original manufacturer's spare part for the DEV-0909 sampling needle has been out of supply, and a substitute part has been used for 3 weeks.
Conclusion: sample degradation and instrument drift cannot be distinguished; none of the four determinations can be accepted; the result is judged as failed and recorded as the unusable tier according to the tiering table; first initiate a deviation investigation before deciding subsequent handling; this batch is temporarily not released, not rerun, and not invalidated.
Note: TK-20261018-7636, which C-51346 has been pressing for, should be transferred to second line first; the matter of the duty colleague being on leave until 2026-11-03 is not on this agenda.

